# Dailies workflows

Dailies drives a real browser from the CLI and records verifiable QA sessions. Set up once with
`npx dailies-cli init` (installs the runtime); browse a session by opening its `report.html`; stop the
shared daemon (and all browsers/sessions) with `npx dailies-cli stop`. For a session, run
`session end <id>` **before** `stop` — `stop` aborts a live session and skips its report.

- **Verify (change → QA plan)** — read a diff, infer the affected user-facing workflows, and suggest
  the flows to test; optionally record them. Skill `dailies-verify` / agent `verify-agent`. Command:
  `/dailies:verify`.
- **Automate (one-off)** — drive a browser and return a result, nothing recorded. Skill
  `dailies-automate` / agent `automate-agent`. Command: `/dailies:run`.
- **Session (recorded QA)** — run scripts as steps that capture trace/video/HAR/console and render
  `report.html`. Skill `dailies-session` / agent `session-agent`. Command: `/dailies:session`.
- **Scripting API** — the sandbox API (`browser.getPage`, page methods, `saveScreenshot`) lives in
  the `dailies-scripting` skill and its `references/REFERENCE.md`.
